We're rushin' outta Russia!

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:39.720
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.760
<b>Shisuka</b>

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:30.330
<b>Episode Thirty-Seven
Rushin' Outta Russia</b>

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.790
I sent a telegram to Lt. Tsurumi

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.380
telling him we have Asirpa 
and have crossed the border.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:03:59.370
Good work.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:03.260
Lieutenant Tsurumi...

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:07.720
I can't wait to see your 
face shining with joy!

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:12.230
I've asked him to send his response 
to the post office at Toyohara.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:17.110
He should want to speak 
to Asirpa as soon as possible.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.570
Let's hurry.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:23.470
Okay, we're leaving!

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.700
We'll go as far as we can before sunset.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.920
Wait.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:28.590
Where did Sugimoto go?

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.780
Okay! Got the miso.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.660
Asirpa-san will be happy, I bet!

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:40.030
You squeezed out a whole 
bunch for me, Sugimoto!

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.470
He was just here.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.550
Where did he go?

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:49.510
Get down!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.720
Shiraishi!

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.630
Shiraishi, can you move?

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.180
Get behind a building!

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.690
They hit my leg!

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:00.120
We'll hide in one of the stores!

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.330
You, too, Asirpa!

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.180
Don't move, Asirpa!

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.240
They hit Shiraishi in the leg

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.780
so they could fire on whoever 
came out of cover to help him!

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.280
Snipers do that all the time.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.750
Snipers...

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.990
Did you get a look at them?

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.320
Keep your head down, Lieutenant Koito!

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.660
Tsukishima, give me your hand mirror!

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:23.090
I'll take a look at them!

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:24.800
Hand... mirror?

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.290
You don't even have a mirror?

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:29.180
That's why your face is so filthy!

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.350
Get it out of my luggage!

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:34.380
I found it.

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.650
You're getting fingerprints on it, fool!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.490
They're firing from a long distance.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.780
Only one person could pull 
off a shot like that!

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:54.180
It's Ogata Hyakunosuke!

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.040
Ogata's back already!

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.550
We're trapped!

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:09.620
What do we do, Tsukishima!

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.850
<i>I'll split open his head 
and fill it with this miso!</i>

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.600
That was Sugimoto!

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.020
I saw him running between the buildings!

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:27.570
Ogata didn't see him?

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:30.200
How could Ogata miss Sugimoto?

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.490
Shiraishi, find some way 
to get your ass over here!

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.420
You'll bleed out if we can't bandage you up!

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:38.980
Shut up!

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:41.920
I've never counted on anybody's help!

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.380
Tanigaki, let's push the sled over to him.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.500
We have to help Shiraishi!

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:47.240
No!

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:50.010
If that's Ogata out there, he's after you!

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.320
I don't care! I have to help!

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.140
Asirpa-chan, stay where you are!

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.430
Hey, doggies!

00:06:56.710 --> 00:07:00.250
Look! Look! Yummy Russian sweets!

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:01.940
Come over here and get them!

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.650
You care about the dogs more than me?

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.400
Crows!

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:13.410
I'll have to throw these into the air 
and let the crows cover my escape!

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.910
Like that!

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:18.910
Go!

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.380
They're so cute...

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.410
<i>I remember him.</i>

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.570
<i>He was there.</i>

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.650
<i>Come on out...</i>

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.760
<i>I didn't get to die last time.</i>

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:37.760
<i>Let's pick up where we left off.</i>

00:07:42.030 --> 00:07:44.180
Are you just messing with the guy?

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.060
I'm keeping him distracted.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:48.190
As part of our plan.

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:50.090
Whose plan?

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.570
What makes a sniper dangerous

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:56.280
is his ability to strike from a distance 
where the enemy can't fire back.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:00.130
Having an enemy approach without them 
realizing is a terrifying thought for a sniper.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:05.700
Especially if that enemy 
is Immortal Sugimoto.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.470
<i>What? Did someone just 
come into the building?</i>

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:14.740
<i>They're close.</i>

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:18.170
<i>I can sense them, like you can feel 
a bear lurking in the undergrowth.</i>

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:23.440
<i>Something dangerous and 
violent is about to strike!</i>

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.380
<i>I'll let him fire a single shot.</i>

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:32.880
<i>Then, in the short gap between 
loading his next bullet</i>

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.390
<i>and putting his finger to the trigger,</i>

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.220
<i>I'll jump him.</i>

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:41.660
<i>With this gun, even if I hit him, 
it won't kill him. He'll shoot back.</i>

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.540
<i>If I want to be sure I've got 
him, I need to get close.</i>

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.080
<i>Ogata...</i>

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.130
<i>I'll finish you myself!</i>

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.210
<i>A mirror?!</i>

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.430
<i>Of course, I'm ready for a close-range fight.</i>

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:09.940
Who the hell are you?

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:15.700
<i>Distance.</i>

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.660
<i>If I can put distance 
between us, I can't lose.</i>

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:34.850
What the hell is this?

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:36.980
Did you draw this?

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.150
You there, stop!

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:43.220
Don't get any closer! You'll be shot! Stop!

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.710
What are the soldiers doing?

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:54.050
Looks like Sugimoto made it.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:55.860
Asirpa!

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.980
Sugimoto!

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:02.110
You friends with Ogata?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.120
Did this man tell you to attack us?

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.500
Where is he?

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:09.500
Where?!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.380
What's this?

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.990
Is that you?

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.230
I see!

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.140
What, you were looking for Ogata?

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:30.650
Oh, because Shiraishi
and Asirpa-san were there...

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.730
These two have nothing to do with it.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.060
It's <i>his</i> fault!

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.860
That's right! Good!

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.740
Ogata shot me, too.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:44.710
You understand?

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:45.820
Bang!

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:48.500
Wait, I'll draw it out for you.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:54.250
Ogata shot me at Abashiri 
Prison and took Asirpa-san away.

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.510
He joined up with Kiroranke 
and shot me and Nopperabo.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:02.760
I don't know when they started 
working together, though.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:06.850
No! He's not a spider!

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:10.580
Asirpa-san's poisoned
arrow hit Ogata in the eye.

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.520
I don't think she intended to shoot him.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:19.280
<b>Ogata ran</b>

00:11:13.940 --> 00:11:16.040
I ripped out his eye to save him.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.920
I didn't want her to bear 
the burden of killing Ogata.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:24.630
When I see Asirpa-san, it almost feels 
like the pure parts of me,

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:29.380
the parts I know I had when I 
was a child, are still there.

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:36.680
Sugimoto, what are you doing?

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:42.330
I think he was one of the 
Russian soldiers that ambushed

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:44.220
Kiroranke Nispa at the border.

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:46.870
This man died.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.200
We don't know where he is. He ran.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.910
We just came to get the child.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:56.170
We have nothing to do with 
the emperor's assassination.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:12:03.690
Mister Russian Soldier, next time you want 
look for someone, ask if he's around first!

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:08.200
He's angry and says you should've 
talked to us before shooting.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:11.190
Don't you have anything to say? 
Is there no word for "sorry" in Russian?

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:12.260
He asks if there's no word 
for "sorry" in Russian.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.590
He can't talk right because of 
his injuries, it looks like.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:25.610
Get your ass back to Russia, asshole.

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.270
That Russian's following us.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.530
He stole a horse.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.910
You think he still suspects us of being 
involved with the emperor's death?

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:48.870
No, he's not interested in 
Kiroranke Nispa anymore.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:53.750
Those drawings were written on 
the back of the wanted poster.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:57.630
So he figures he can find 
Ogata if he stays close to us?

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.700
He probably plans to keep going 
until one of them is dead.

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:03.720
"If I'm not dead, I haven't lost," he thinks.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.720
Do you think Ogata will come back?

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:11.530
He might, if you're the key 
to cracking the gold code.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:15.180
But he looked like he was trying to kill me.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.020
Is the gold what he's after, really?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:28.460
He might just be trying 
to mess with us, yeah.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:32.040
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.020
Only Sofia can tell us the full truth.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.900
I'd love to go to the continent 
to search for her, but...

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:46.580
The 7th Division doesn't 
care about any of that.

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:50.440
Their top priority is bringing Asirpa-san back.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:56.430
And Tanigaki came here so he could bring 
Asirpa-san to Huci and help her feel better.

00:13:57.260 --> 00:13:59.180
The plan that Kiroranke Nispa and Sofia had

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:02.900
was to gather comrades on the 
continent and then come to Japan.

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:06.610
Sofia's not the kind of person to 
run to the continent and stay there.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:23.570
<b>ABASHIRI</b>

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:23.570
<b>LAKE AKAN</b>

00:14:19.230 --> 00:14:21.010
<i>The area around Lake Akan</i>

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:25.140
<i>was filled with laborers working in the 
coal mines and salmon fishing trade.</i>

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.380
<i>A town had been built for them.</i>

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:34.310
<b>Inn</b>

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:34.310
Ushiyama and Hijikata-san disappeared 
without a word two days ago.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.930
Something must have happened to them.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:40.010
Maybe they found some pretty girls?

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:44.020
Even if something did happen, 
those two are unbeatable.

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:50.690
Fine. You wait here, Nagakura-san.

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:52.360
Let's go, Kirawus.

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:56.370
<b>Inn</b>

00:14:56.730 --> 00:15:00.670
Perhaps they went after the prisoner who's 
said to be in hiding near Lake Akan,

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.330
and he killed them.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.600
Those two?

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:11.050
Well, sure. He's worthless 
in a fight, but he is clever.

00:15:11.460 --> 00:15:14.140
You know him, Kadokura?

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.650
I used to be his jailer, you know.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:22.350
I know the wrinkles in his asshole 
better than I know his face.

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:24.110
The wrinkles in his asshole?

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:27.210
He was a former vet.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:30.360
He'd go around and look at horses and 
farm animals all around Hokkaido.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:37.690
Sekiya Waichiro said he used the strychnine 
that's used to exterminate Ezo wolves,

00:15:37.690 --> 00:15:42.030
potassium cyanide, arsenic, 
and other poisons to kill 30 men.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.790
<b>Cellblock Four</b>

00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:46.190
You can hide the bitterness with miso.

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:50.300
I've put poison into one of these three 
bowls of miso soup to see what would happen.

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.160
Wolfsbane is bitter, though.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:57.220
He said it tasted weird as he ate it.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:01.850
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:06.820
I can tell you're a yakuza boss, 
since you've got good luck.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:09.320
I like testing people's luck.

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:12.240
And the ones with bad luck, I kill.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:18.040
Sekiya had snagged some 
wolfsbane while he was on work

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:21.970
detail outside the prison 
and snuck it back in.

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:29.710
After that, it was my job to look inside 
his asshole whenever he came back to jail.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:34.080
If you stuck that stuff up your ass,
 the poison would kill you.

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:36.590
He wouldn't hide it there.

00:16:36.590 --> 00:16:38.120
You're a moron.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:44.640
I looked inside his asshole for nothing.

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:50.590
Annu. Annu.

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.240
I'm looking for a man with 
a bump on his forehead

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:56.530
and a Japanese with long white hair.

00:16:56.800 --> 00:16:57.800
Don't know 'em.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.200
Kirawus!

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.570
There's another Ainu down 
that way. Go ask them.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:08.270
Don't tell me what to do, asshole-peeker.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:11.650
I work for your boss, you know.

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.880
I'm stuck in middle management 
forever, aren't I?

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:23.900
You, fat kid.

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:25.140
Hold up a second.

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:29.520
You see a scary-looking guy with 
white hair, looks like a monster?

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.340
What do you think?

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:33.530
About what?

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.860
I've seen a foreigner 
dance before in Hakodate.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:41.030
Don't you think it would be wonderful 
if you could dance while skating?

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.630
An incredible invention, isn't it?

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:46.830
<i>This was the birth of Japan's 
first figure skater!</i>

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.580
Yeah, whatever.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:51.190
I saw that man.

00:17:51.850 --> 00:17:54.210
He was standing over there, just yesterday.

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:56.500
Right in this area?

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:01.810
This is...

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:05.870
You see those silkworm cocoons, yes?

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:13.270
Half of them contain fugu poison, 
arsenic, wolfsbane, strychnine.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:16.350
Half of them, however, are "winners" 
that have no poison at all.

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:18.860
Take one and I'll release Ushiyama.

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:21.510
I'm not interested in games.

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:24.290
I'm about to chase you 
to the ends of the earth,

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.290
and then rip the flesh off your living body.

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:29.520
You're Hijikata Toshizou, aren't you?

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:34.790
What's a man like you trying to 
do with the gold? I'm curious.

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:38.220
<i>So he has a horse with him?</i>

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.930
<i>He'll be able to flee.</i>

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:44.010
I paralyzed Ushiyama with a small 
amount of fugu poison,

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:46.810
gave him datura to make him pass out,
 and buried him in a coffin.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:51.710
There's an air hole, but 
he can't even drink water.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:54.860
You don't have time to chase 
after me, I don't think.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.940
I've already made a copy of his tattoos.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:03.530
When I told him I'd kidnapped you 
and buried you, he took one of them.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:09.170
If you're following the right path, 
you should be blessed with good luck.

00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.490
Men make their own luck.

00:19:11.490 --> 00:19:14.200
And if you make the wrong choice, 
that means your path was wrong.

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:17.880
Try your luck.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:30.880
There was enough of each poison to be lethal.

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:33.350
Amazing. He's still alive.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:39.610
From the symptoms, he took 
the fugu tetrodotoxin.

00:19:39.940 --> 00:19:45.330
His comrades will give the tattooed 
skins they have to get back Hijikata.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.290
I need to hide him somewhere else.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.270
What is this?

00:19:57.610 --> 00:20:01.610
What the fat boy saw, and then 
this mysterious white shell...

00:20:01.610 --> 00:20:04.370
I see, I see!

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:08.210
This case has gone completely cold!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.170
Hey, you.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:17.270
I'm here for salmon, but all 
I'm catching is pond smelt.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:20.040
I can't eat them all. Want some?

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:21.650
Thanks.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:24.740
Fry them into tempura and 
eat them with your friends.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:28.820
The salmon start getting active in late fall.

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:30.950
You can't catch many this time of year.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:33.290
You're not from around here, are you?

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.330
Nope.

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:40.170
Kadokura, somebody gave me a bunch of chika.

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:42.440
Oh, smelt?

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:45.790
Let's go back to the inn and eat 
them while we wait for their return.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:47.100
We're leaving already?

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:54.770
<i>I put a lethal amount of tetrodotoxin 
in the mouth of one of them.</i>

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:58.020
<i>It's a deadly poison that remains 
potent even after grilling or boiling.</i>

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:01.540
<i>Will you be given blessings or judgment?</i>

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:05.780
The choice you make will determine your fate.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:21.220
No way.

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:23.780
Sorry, Kirawus.

00:21:23.780 --> 00:21:25.780
They were such a nice gift, too.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:27.260
No, I mean...

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:30.140
It's fine, I get it.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.470
My luck's just like that.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:35.290
There'll be a wildfire, and my house 
is the only one to burn down.

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:38.300
And when I was in middle school, 
40 of us were out walking,

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:41.480
and I was the one guy to fall 
into a snow-covered cesspit.

00:21:41.480 --> 00:21:43.780
I'm always like that.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.820
I was born under a bad star.

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:55.040
<i>Former Head Jailer Kadokura 
possesses horrifically bad luck!</i>

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time
Cocoon</b>

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:38.500
Next time: "Cocoon"!
